{"version":1,"basis":"Order follows the chronology of James Ussher, Annals of the World (1650; creation 4004 BC), with the KJV text taken as literally accurate, and the traditional conservative harmony for placements Ussher leaves open. Parallel accounts (Samuel/Kings/Chronicles, Kings/Isaiah/Jeremiah, the four Gospels) are read side by side, every verse once. Psalms sit with the events of their superscriptions (untitled ones with the period their content fits); prophets in the reigns they name. Choices: Job in the patriarchal era after Genesis 50, before the Exodus; Judges 17-21 right after Joshua (Phinehas still priest); Ruth early in the judges (Boaz son of Rahab); Obadiah under Jehoram and Joel under Joash (early dates); Proverbs, Song and Ecclesiastes with Solomon; Daniel 3 after the fall of Jerusalem (LXX 18th year); Esther between Ezra 6 and 7 (Ussher identified Ahasuerus with Darius Hystaspes, so Esther overlaps Ezra 5-6); Malachi with Nehemiah 13; the Gospels in one harmony; Epistles inserted into Acts where written (James before the council, Galatians and 1-2 Thessalonians on the second journey, Hebrews before AD 70, John's letters and Revelation last).","order":[[1001001,1002025],[1003001,1005032],[13001001,13001004],[1006001,1009029],[1010001,1011009],[1011010,1011032],[13001005,13001027],[1012001,1014024],[1015001,1016016],[1017001,1020018],[1021001,1024067],[1025001,1025018],[13001028,13001033],[1025019,1025034],[1026001,1028022],[1029001,1031055],[1032001,1035029],[1036001,1036043],[13001034,13001054],[1037001,1040023],[1041001,1044034],[1045001,1047031],[1048001,1050026],[18001001,18002013],[18003001,18006030],[18007001,18010022],[18011001,18014022],[18015001,18018021],[18019001,18021034],[18022001,18025006],[18026001,18029025],[18030001,18031040],[18032001,18034037],[18035001,18037024],[18038001,18040024],[18041001,18042017],[2001001,2003022],[2004001,2006030],[2007001,2009035],[2010001,2012051],[2013001,2015027],[2016001,2018027],[2019001,2021036],